    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0868" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7435 Amateur/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Argentine Ministry for Foreign Affairs to the
                        American Embassy in Argentina </hi><anchor n="7" xml:id="d623-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Worship addresses the Embassy of the United
                    States of America, and with reference to its note <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Aide-Mémoire</hi> dated February 28 last, concerning the proposed
                    modification of Radio Regulations of Madrid in so far as it concerns amateurs,
                    takes pleasure in enclosing copy of the report issued by <pb facs="0869" n="769"
                        xml:id="pg769"/> the office in charge of the control of radio communications
                    in the country, which the pertinent Department has adopted in all its parts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1934-08-07">August 7,
                            1934</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d623-a1.xml" xpointer="d623-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d623-f1" n="7" type="source" xml:id="d623-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in Argentina in his despatch
                    No. 401, August 29; received September 10.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
